{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The spade connector kit matches the kind I previously bought, so it feels like a practical replenishment for familiar wiring repairs.",
    "The clear duct tape fits my repeated purchases of repair tape while offering a less visible patch, and the wire harness tape connects that repair interest with my electrical connector purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Large battery cable lugs and a power distribution block require specific projects I have not indicated; buying spade connectors does not mean I currently need those parts.",
    "The T-tap connectors are relevant to wiring, but I would choose the familiar spade kit this time. The hooks, spray bottles, and bulk masks do not address a repair need I have right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My electrical supply purchases seem to have been taken as interest in many kinds of electrical hardware, even when their purpose and fit differ.",
    "General usefulness seems to count too much: an item being handy to keep around is not enough for me to buy it now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The specific connector style matters to me more than a broad connection to wiring supplies.",
    "I am more interested in replenishing familiar repair materials or adding a clear repair benefit than in starting an unrelated project or stocking up on bulk supplies."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in tape and wiring repairs but stretched it into supplies for needs I have not expressed."
}"}
